===BODY===
          <h2>Quick to bring home</h2>
          <p>The E40 motorway runs from Brussels past Ghent and Bruges to the French border near Dunkirk, and on to Calais. From most of Belgium, the Channel is only a few hours away, which makes repatriation from Belgium one of the fastest options.</p>

          <h2>Where we collect from</h2>
          <p>We collect from anywhere in Belgium: Brussels, Antwerp, Ghent, Bruges, the coast, Leuven, Liège, Namur and the Ardennes. Cars at a garage, a pound, a hotel car park or by the roadside after local recovery are all fine.</p>

          <h2>Dutch and French spoken</h2>
          <p>Belgium has two main languages, and we speak both. We can arrange collection directly with the garage or recovery company, in Dutch in Flanders and in French in Brussels and Wallonia.</p>

          <div class="callout">
            <p><strong>Low emission zones:</strong> Brussels, Antwerp and Ghent have low emission zones, and foreign cars generally need to be registered before driving in. That doesn't affect us collecting a broken-down car, but check before you drive into these cities.</p>
          </div>
===FAQ===
Q: Can you deal with the Belgian garage for me?
A: Yes. We speak Dutch and French, so we can arrange collection directly with the garage. Just give us their name and number.
Q: How long does it take?
A: From Belgium it's usually one of our quickest repatriations. We'll confirm the expected timing when we quote.
Q: Can you bring back an accident-damaged car?
A: Yes, including cars that don't roll. Tell us when you ask for a quote.
